==Trivia==

* Ashe's dance references [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G4LIM9VYhB0 J'en Ai Marre!] by {{w|Alizée}}.
** A side by side comparison can be seen [http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v3iyKHLrv_I here.]
* Ashe shares similarities with {{wikia|FinalFantasy|Ashelia B'nargin Dalmasca}} from {{w|Final Fantasy XII}}. Their names are similar and both became queens, use ranged weapons (Ashelia uses hand bombs in {{w|Final Fantasy XII: Revenant Wings}}) and were once hunted down to prevent them from leading their respective peoples.
* Ashe is the first (and so far the only) champion to possess two global-ranged abilities: {{ai|Hawkshot|Ashe}} and {{ai|Enchanted Crystal Arrow|Ashe}}.
** {{ai|Timewinder|Ekko}} and {{ais|Chronobreak|Ekko}} ranges can be global, albeit situationally.
* Ashe was named for [[Marc 'Tryndamere' Merrill]]'s wife Ashley.
* As of December 9, 2017 Ashe has featured on the [[free champion rotation]] more than any other champion (76 times).
* In [[Summoner's Rift]], {{ii|Thornmail}} was once recommended as a situational item for {{ci|Ashe}}, this was most likely a reference to the old [[Tutorial|Basic Tutorial]] where {{ci|Ashe}} is pre-selected as the player's champion and {{ii|Thornmail}} is the only purchasable item.
* In the now-removed official League of Legends [https://web.archive.org/web/20130726165848/http://forums.na.leagueoflegends.com/board/ forums], the [[File:Focus_old.png|20px]] old icon of {{cci|Focus.png|Ashe/LoL/History#Previous_Abilities|Focus}} was used to represent the "New Player Forum" section.

