==Trivia==
* {{Champion with infinite scaling|Cho'Gath}}
** In Cho'Gath's case, {{ai|Feast|Cho'Gath}} infinitely stacks his {{as|health}}.
* Cho'Gath was the first [[champion]] to receive a second {{skin tier|Legendary}} [[skin]] (though {{ci|Corki}} has two {{RP|1820}} skins both of which are [[Legacy Vault|Legacy]] and {{ci|Tristana}} has also two {{RP|1820}} skins although one is Legacy and the other one is available).
* Cho'Gath's dance references {{w|Fantasmic!}} by {{w|Mickey Mouse}}.
* [[Riot Games|Riot]] created an {{w|Adobe Flash}} minigame dedicated for him called [[Cho'Gath Eats the World]] for [[April Fools' Day]] [[Season 3|2013]].
** Another minigame released on the same date, [[Astro Teemo]], which was unlocked by playing to a certain point in this game.
* The depiction of Cho'Gath in the [[File:Feral_Scream.png|20px]] icon of {{ai|Feral Scream|Cho'Gath}}  was based on his pose in his {{csl|Cho'Gath|Original|Original splash art}}.
* In the now-removed official League of Legends [https://web.archive.org/web/20130726165848/http://forums.na.leagueoflegends.com/board/ forums], the [[File:Feral_Scream_old.png|20px]] original icon of {{ai|Feral Scream|Cho'Gath}} was used to represent the "General Discussion" section.
* In the official League of Legends game [https://youtu.be/0vKpfxHU6oc?t=36 trailer] from 2009, Cho'Gath was given generic T-Rex sounds.
* In the [[April Fool's Patch 2011|V1.0.0.115]] [[April Fools' Day]] patch;
** The following changes regarding Cho'Gath were jokingly listed：
*** Cho'Gath now starts the game the same size as if he had 6 {{ai|Feast|Cho'Gath|variant=old|feasts}}.
*** {{ai|Feast|Cho'Gath|variant=old}} still increases Cho'Gath's size.
*** {{tip|brush|Bushes}} can no longer {{tip|stealth}} Cho'Gath.
** The following joke item was listed to be added:
*** NEW Yordle Saddle: Any [[yordle]] champion can buy this new item to ride Cho'Gath.
* Cho'Gath was given a retexture and features as a monster called the "Big Stompy Monster" (along with its huge variant) in {{tip|Invasion}}, a [[featured game mode]].


