==Trivia==

* Amumu's original icon for {{ai|Bandage Toss|Amumu|image=Bandage Toss old.png}} shows him in a pose that references {{w|Spider-Man}}'s web shooting from {{w|Marvel Comics}}.
* Amumu is seen on a caution sign in the game's Mac Version trailer.
* Amumu was the third [[champion]] to attain 7 [[skins]].
* Amumu's dance references the Goth kids' [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mT8vwGXGEDc&t=1s dance] from ''{{w|South Park}}'' adult animated series.
** A side-by-side comparison can be seen [http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S4VGVeAwQ8U here.]
** Both are in turn parodying classic '[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s1LUXQWzCno Peanut's Dance]', a bizarre shuffling dance performed by the characters from the {{w|Peanuts}} comic and animated films.
* When Amumu dies, his pose is that of an Egyptian {{w|mummy}} with his arms crossed right over left.
** This is a nod to him being a [[Shurima]]n boy prince in life.
* Amumu's price range was lowered from {{IP|1350}} to {{IP|450}} in accordance with the release of his [[The Curse of the Sad Mummy]] music video.
* Amumu and {{ci|Blitzcrank}} were [http://www.surrenderat20.net/2017/01/110-pbe-update.html#newskins planned] to have {{csl|Amumu|Sewn Chaos|Sewn}} {{csl|Blitzcrank|Sewn Chaos|Chaos}} skins, but both were [[Unreleased Content|cancelled]] for [https://web.archive.org/web/0/http://boards.pbe.leagueoflegends.com/en/c/general-pbe-feedback/qnK0MB8Q-update-on-sewn-chaos failing] to meet [[Riot Games Inc.|Riot]]'s quality standards.
** They may return in the future.
* The [[ward skin]] {{cci|Sad Mummy Ward.png||''Sad Mummy Ward''|border=false}} references him.
* He has a base size of 50 which is considered medium.

