==Trivia==

;{{ci|Dr. Mundo|variant=old2|image=Dr. Mundo OriginalSquare old2.png|Dr. Mundo, the Madman of Zaun|size=32}}
* "Mundo" has two real world origins: the Proto-Germanic ''*mundo'' "hand, protection" & unrelated Ibero-{{w|Romance languages|Romance}} ''mundo'' "world" (like in Spanish, Portuguese, etc.).
** He is named after [[Edmundo 'odnumde' Sanchez]], by [[Brandon 'Ryze' Beck]].<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/0/http://www.leagueoflegends.com/board/showthread.php?t=872817 Mundo Name Origin]</ref>
* Dr. Mundo's dance references the titular character from {{w|House, M.D.}} in turn dancing to [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8PaoLy7PHwk Fight the Power] by {{w|Public Enemy (band)|Public Enemy}}.
** A side-by-side comparison be seen [http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HpzBLUDnQik here].
* In the [[April Fool's Patch 2011|V1.0.0.115]] [[April Fools' Day]] patch, the following change regarding Dr. Mundo were jokingly listed：
** Dr. Mundo decided that he enjoys the color blue.
** Dr. Mundo now has mana.
** None of his ability costs have changed.
* {{ai|Masochism|Dr. Mundo}} references the {{w|Masochism|eponymous term}} for enjoyment derived from being inflicted pain, named after real-life writer {{w|Leopold von Sacher-Masoch}}.
** This is also mechanically referenced in his kit by gaining a higher AD bonus the lower his health is.
** The ability's name also fits for the {{cci|Masochism_old.png|Dr._Mundo/LoL/History#Previous_Abilities|early iterations}} of his E ability, which caused Dr. Mundo to be healed instead of being damaged from physical attacks for a duration.
* {{ai|Sadism|Dr. Mundo}} references the {{w|Sadism|eponymous term}} for enjoyment derived from inflicting pain on others, named after real-life writer {{w|Marquis de Sade}}.
** The name chosen for this ability made the most sense for the {{cci|Kiss of Death.png|Dr._Mundo/LoL/History#Previous_Abilities|early iterations}} of his R ability, which damaged nearby enemies for their current health.

;{{ci|Dr. Mundo|Dr. Mundo, the Madman of Zaun|size=32}}
* {{Champion without ability power ratio|Dr. Mundo}}
* Dr. Mundo is one of six champions who use health as a resource for abilities, the other five being {{ci|Briar}}, {{ci|Olaf}}, {{ci|Soraka}},  {{ci|Vladimir}} and {{ci|Zac}}.
* His dance is a [https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PecFlex Pec Flex] which involves flexing his pectoral muscles.
* His [[death]] animation shows him assume the morgue pose whilst adding a toe tag to himself.
* {{ai|Goes Where He Pleases|Dr. Mundo}} is among a few abilities that were named after a quote of their champion. In this case, it references his "Mundo goes where he pleases" quote which he had before the patch he got the ability, [[V11.12]].
** The others are {{cai|League of Draven|Draven}} and {{cai|End of the Line|Graves}}.
* Following his rework, his kit was given a higher emphasis on medical equipment and terms, thus making several references to them.
** {{ai|Infected Bonesaw|Dr. Mundo}} was renamed from {{ai|Infected Cleaver|Dr. Mundo}} to have Dr. Mundo utilize the {{w|Bone cutter|actual medical tool}}.
** {{ai|Heart Zapper|Dr. Mundo}} is based on the act of {{w|defibrillation}}.
** {{ai|Blunt Force Trauma|Dr. Mundo}} references the term for the {{w|blunt trauma|eponymous injury type}}.

