==Trivia==
* {{Shapeshifter Champion|Elise}}
** In Elise's case, {{ai|Spider Form / Human Form|Elise}} allows her to freely switch between her melee {{sbc|Spider Form}} and her ranged {{sbc|Human Form}}, both having their specific sets of abilities.
* Elise, {{ci|Nidalee}}, {{ci|Gnar}}, {{ci|Jayce}} and {{ci|Kayle}} are the only champions to be conditionally considered both {{tip|ranged}} and {{tip|melee}}.
* She was the first champion to have a monologue during her login screen, the others being (in that order) {{ci|Lissandra}}, {{ci|Lucian}}, and {{ci|Yasuo}}.
* She is one of the few champions to have:
** Access to both her {{ai|Spider Form|Elise|ultimate}} and a basic ability at level 1 (the others being {{ci|Karma}}, {{ci|Jayce}}, and {{ci|Nidalee}}).
** A total of 19 ranks across all abilities at level 18 (the others being {{ci|Jayce}}, {{ci|Karma}}, {{ci|Nidalee}}, and {{ci|Yuumi}}).
** Her transformation available before level 6 (the others being {{ci|Gnar}}, {{ci|Jayce}}, and {{ci|Nidalee}}).
** More than five abilities (the others including {{ci|Gnar}}, {{ci|Hwei}}, {{ci|Jayce}}, {{ci|Kled}}, {{ci|Lee Sin}}, {{ci|Nidalee}}, and {{ci|Rek'Sai}}).
** Her title as the name of one of her abilities (the others being {{cai|The Darkin Blade|Aatrox}}, {{cai|Grandmaster-at-Arms|Jax}}, {{cai|Fury of the North|Sejuani}}, {{cai|Night Hunter|Vayne}}, and {{cai|The Relentless Storm|Volibear}}).
* Elise's dance is the [http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rx8ERVLUAFY Can-can].
** A side-by-side comparison of both her forms can be seen [http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W0d9J8ydaNA here.]
** She shares this dance with {{csl|Veigar|Final Boss}} and {{ci|Urgot}}.
* Elise's {{ai|Spider Form|Elise}} {{si|Recall|recalling}} might be referencing [https://zeldawiki.wiki/wiki/Skulltula Skulltula] from {{w|The Legend of Zelda}}.
* Elise was the base for [[Twisted Treeline (League of Legends)|Twisted Treeline's]] 2012 update, at whose center {{ui|Vilemaw|her god}} would reside.
* Elise is the final incarnation of {{ui|Priscilla}}, a [[Unreleased Content|canceled]] champion brought back by playerbase request.

