==Trivia==
* {{Champion with infinite scaling|Aurelion Sol}}
** In Aurelion Sol's case, {{as|Stardust|soul}} stacks gained through {{ai|I|Aurelion Sol}} permanently increases {{ai|Q|Aurelion Sol}}'s bonus {{as|magic damage}}, {{ai|W|Aurelion Sol}}'s range, {{ai|E|Aurelion Sol}}'s outer and inner radius and execution threshold and {{ai|R|Aurelion Sol}} and {{ai|The Skies Descend|Aurelion Sol}}'s effect radius.
* {{ai|The Skies Descend|Aurelion Sol}} was named after his champion spell of the same {{LoR|The Skies Descend|name}} in {{tip|Legends of Runeterra}}.
* In 'Aurelion Sol: The Star Forger Returns' his hand gesture resembles the old [[Riot Games Inc.]] fist intro.
* A lot of his animations and visual effects were inspired by {{w|Astronomical object|celestial objects}} and {{w|Atom|atoms}}.
* Aurelion Sol's lower body is not part of his in-game [[Unit_radius#Gameplay_radius|hitbox]], which is why it is semi-transparent.
** A demonstration can be seen [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eDJcYk4b8Vw here].
* Prior to his CGU, in [[Ultra Rapid Fire]] his {{ai|Center of the Universe|Aurelion Sol}} passive used to have 6 stars orbiting around him with increased speed, simply by leveling up.
** Interestingly, this is the only non-stat modification made to any champion in URF, suggesting this may have originally been an intended feature which was scrapped from the champion before release.
* The name of the concept character from which Aurelion Sol spurred from, ​​​​​​{{ui|Ao Shin}}, could be a reference to {{w|Dragon_King#Red_Dragon|Ao Qin}}, the ''{{w|Dragon King}} of the {{w|South China Sea|South Sea}}''.
* Aurelion Sol's Series 1 and 2 [[Eternals]] make the following references:
** ''Spaghettification'' is a reference to the homonym {{w|Spaghettification|concept}} in astrophysics that refers to objects becoming vertically stretched and horizontally compressed in very strong gravitational fields, such as black holes.
** ''Flying in the 90s'' is a reference to the song [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8WEe-MmC4ag Running in the 90s] by italian singer {{wikia|eurobeat|Maurizio De Jorio}}.
* Aurelion Sol's temporary internal name was "Heaven's Coil" which was chosen to intentionally be a "god-awful temp name."<ref>League of Legends Nexus — Riot BananaBandit (26 December 2017) [https://nexus.leagueoflegends.com/en-us/2017/12/naming-new-champions/ Naming New Champions]</ref>

