==Trivia==
* The icon for {{ai|The Hitman and the Seer|Aphelios}} changes based on the active skin and functions as '''Alune's''' portrait, similarly to '''Aphelios' '''portrait.
* {{ci|Aphelios}} and {{cbi|Alune}} are possibly inspired by the {{w|Proto-Indo-European_mythology#Sun_and_Moon|Sun and Moon twins}} from {{w|Proto-Indo-European mythology|Indo-European mythology}}, although {{Tt|both twins|though Aphelios is related to a real-life heliological term}} belong to the Lunari order.
* Aphelios is the first and only champion to have fewer than five abilities.
* A unique HUD is used due to the unorthodox arrangement of his kit.
* Aphelios has a game start ceremony that forces him in place.
* Because of his innate ability, Aphelios is able to obtain the highest amount of [[lethality]] out of any champion and effect combination in [[League of Legends]].
* Aphelios' ''{{ai|Severum|Aphelios}}'' attack has the highest missile speed on an attack out of any champion, at 92400.
** This is by far higher than the second one, which is {{cai|Cultivation of Spirit|Yunara}} attacks at 10000.
* Since Aphelios can hold two weapons at a time with {{ai|The Hitman and the Seer|Aphelios}}, there are {{tt|10 different possible combinations|(5!)/[(2!)*(5-2)!]}} of weapons he can have equipped. These are:
*# {{ai|Calibrum|Aphelios}} and {{ai|Severum|Aphelios}}
*# {{ai|Calibrum|Aphelios}} and {{ai|Gravitum|Aphelios}}
*# {{ai|Calibrum|Aphelios}} and {{ai|Infernum|Aphelios}}
*# {{ai|Calibrum|Aphelios}} and {{ai|Crescendum|Aphelios}}
*# {{ai|Severum|Aphelios}} and {{ai|Gravitum|Aphelios}}
*# {{ai|Severum|Aphelios}} and {{ai|Infernum|Aphelios}}
*# {{ai|Severum|Aphelios}} and {{ai|Crescendum|Aphelios}}
*# {{ai|Gravitum|Aphelios}} and {{ai|Infernum|Aphelios}}
*# {{ai|Gravitum|Aphelios}} and {{ai|Crescendum|Aphelios}}
*# {{ai|Infernum|Aphelios}} and {{ai|Crescendum|Aphelios}}
* Some of Aphelios' ability names are modified by an adjective based on the current {{as|off-hand weapon}}, both for flavor and to signify their applied effect (therefore {{ai|Moonshot|Aphelios}}, {{ai|Onslaught|Aphelios}}, {{ai|Duskwave|Aphelios}} and {{ai|Sentry|Aphelios}}).
** {{ai|Calibrum|Aphelios}} = ''Precision''
** {{ai|Severum|Aphelios}} = ''Resurgent''
** {{ai|Gravitum|Aphelios}} = ''Binding''
** {{ai|Infernum|Aphelios}} = ''Incendiary''
** {{ai|Crescendum|Aphelios}} = ''Arcing''
** Note that {{ai|Moonlight Vigil|Aphelios}} does not include this modifier because it applies the more obvious, {{as|main weapon's}} effect.
* Aphelios was associated with a meme known as [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eeMBHy6j69E '200 years'] that stemmed from a champion designer's controversial [https://twitter.com/Lutzburg/status/1215043827586588672 comments] regarding game design experience. Despite the comment being in response to a conversation about {{ci|Wukong}}, the meme has been affiliated with Aphelios because the comment was made shortly after Aphelios's release, because Aphelios's kit was complex in both visual clarity and mechanics, and because Aphelios was extraordinarily strong at release.
* Aphelios' dance references “[https://youtu.be/UXAdlaUhrlE Senorita (choreography version)]” by [https://www.famousbirthdays.com/people/austin-pak.html Austin Pak] & [https://www.famousbirthdays.com/people/may-j-lee.html May J. Lee].
* Aphelios' Series 2 [[Eternals]] make the following references:
** ''Perfectly Balanced'' is a reference to {{wikia|marvel|Thanos (Earth-199999)|Thanos}} from ''{{w|Avengers: Infinity War}}''.

